      "message": "It only fails on arm64 because the ABI on x86 is not enforced.\nIt only fails on the kernel_virt_aarch64 target because those are building modules. Apparently, the config option also affects the modules (the virtual targets inherit the gki_defconfig). __page_pinner_migration_failed needs to be added to a symbol list (use build/build_abi.sh --update-symbol-list on the cuttlefish device build to generate the update. This un-un-exports the symbol in the GKI kernel. You also need to update the abi.xml in the GKI kernel (build/build_abi.sh for the GKI kernel) after having done the symbol list update to incorporate the new symbols in the ABI representation.",
